// The computer against the computer (WP9.5a, docs/rules/ai.md "AI against AI"): the map `assets/maps/m1` and
// the start of `m1_ai.ron` (a construction centre and 4000 credits each, the south-west and the north-east
// start site), but BOTH players are under `controller: Ai(profile: "normal")`.
//
// Headless only. The game refuses an AI on the local seat (docs/rules/match.md: the local player takes its
// orders from the keyboard), so `sf_game --match m1_duel` stops with that error. It is played by
// `sf_headless tournament assets/matches/m1_duel.ron`, which plays it many times: the factions and the
// seeds of a game are the tool's to vary (the faction written here is game 0's seat 0 and seat 1; the tool
// swaps them, mirrors included), and the first game of a run is this file as it stands.
// A player is defeated when it owns no standing construction centre (WP7.7), as in m1.
(
    name: "m1_duel",
    map: "m1",
    seed: 458758,
    players: [
        (
            id: 0,
            faction: Meridian,
            credits: 4000,
            objects: [
                (role: "construction_center", cell: (12, 68)),
            ],
            controller: Ai(profile: "normal"),
        ),
        (
            id: 1,
            faction: Veyran,
            credits: 4000,
            objects: [
                (role: "construction_center", cell: (72, 14)),
            ],
            controller: Ai(profile: "normal"),
        ),
    ],
)
